# Mirrors the routing done locally by Azoom Server/serve-all.mjs, since
# Netlify only serves static files (it can't run that custom Node server).
# Order matters — first match wins, so the sub-site rules must come before
# the catch-all root rule.

# Malaysia and Egypt use client-side routing (React Router) — any deep link
# that isn't a real built file falls back to that site's own index.html so
# React Router can take over (e.g. /malaysia/contact, /egypt/fees).
/malaysia/*  /malaysia/index.html  200
/egypt/*     /egypt/index.html     200

# Rwanda, Global, and the Hub are single-page sites — no deep sub-routes
# needed, but this keeps a direct hit on any stray sub-path working too.
/rwanda/*    /rwanda/index.html    200
/global/*    /global/index.html    200

# Hub itself, at the root.
/*           /index.html           200
